Tidy← {
⍝H Tidy (fn)  
⍝H ∘  Aligns comments nicely in dfn or tradfn source (and code generally),
⍝H    distinguishing between left-hand side (LHS) comments and right-hand 
⍝H    side (RHS), so that RHS comments can be aligned all together.
⍝H ∘  Unlike other similar software, it can locate the comments in any 
⍝H    desired column and by default calculates a "best" position, for cases
⍝H    where only a few code lines are longish (> 50 characters). 
⍝H ∘  Handles arbitrary char. vectors of vectors, files, and in-workspace 
⍝H    fns and ops.
⍝H ----------------------
⍝H {res}← [opts] ∇ source                 
⍝H   source: [sourceDoc(depth 2) | sourceFnOp(depth 1) | sourceFi(depth 1)]
⍝H   opts: ( 
⍝H      ⍝ Default options. ¨col¨, target column for RHS comments, has many options.    
⍝H        col: 'best' ⋄  min: 20 ⋄ fi: 0  ⋄ updt: 1 ⋄ dbl: 1 ⋄ inc: 5  
⍝H        pctile: 95 ⋄ compact: 50 ⋄ marg: 2 5   
⍝H   )
⍝H   res:    the modified source document as a shy char vector of vectors result. 
⍝H           As the default "side" effect, Tidy by default updates a named
⍝H           fn, op, or file IN PLACE (updt: 1). 
⍝  For the rest of this HELP info, see bottom of this function or do Tidy⍨'help' 
  1 22 911:: ⎕SIGNAL⊂⎕DMX.('EN'EN ⋄ 'Message'Message)
    ⍝ Initialise
      ⎕IO ⎕ML← 0 1
      ⍺← ()
    'help'≡⎕C⍺: ⎕ED 'h'⊣ h← '^\s*⍝H\s?(.*)' ⎕S ' \1'⊢ ⎕NR ⊃⎕XSI 
    ⍝ Variables, defined  
      fnOpÊ←  ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown function or operator' )
      optÊ←   ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown option(s)' )
      colÊ←   ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Invalid column value' )
      fixÊ←   ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Can''t fix object' )
      logicÊ← ⊂( 'EN' 911 ⋄ 'Message' 'Logic error' )
      o← (                                  ⍝ Default options    
        col: 'best' ⋄  min: 20 ⋄ fi: 0  ⋄ updt: 1 ⋄ dbl: 1 ⋄ inc: 5  
        pctile: 95 ⋄ compact: 50 ⋄ marg: 2 5   
      )
      _← o ⎕NS ⍺                            ⍝ Merge in user options
    ×≢⊃~/(⍺ o).⎕NL ¯2: ⎕SIGNAL optÊ         ⍝ Does user bring only valid options?            
    ⍝ Functions (Part I). 
    ⍝ Note: namespace o is an implicit arg of all fns
      ∆Tidy← ∇                              ⍝ This function ("me")
      FOF← {                                ⍝ FOF: in-core fn/op or file?
        ~o.fi: _← {                         ⍝ File with code of any type
            ~⍵ ⎕NC⍛∊ 3 4: ⎕SIGNAL fnOpÊ
              ll← o ∆Tidy 62 ⎕ATX ⍵         ⍝ Get ⍵ and process.  
            ~o.updt: _← ll                  ⍝ No update here. Return the lines.
            0≠ ⊃0⍴⎕FX ll: _← ll             ⍝ Update the fn/op and return the lines..
              ⎕SIGNAL fixÊ 
        }⍵
            o.fi← 0                         ⍝ In-core function
            ll← o ∆Tidy ⊃⎕NGET ⍵ 1          ⍝ Get and process
            _← ll⊂⍛⎕NPUT⍣o.updt⊢ ⍵ 1        ⍝  Update the file. (if o.updt=1) 
        1: _← ll     
      }
    1≥≡ ⍵: FOF ,⍵                           ⍝ FOF handles fns (fi:0), files (fi:1).
    ⍝ Functions (Part II)
      AL← {                                 ⍝ AL: Align line
          ∆ p← ⍺ ⍵                          ⍝ ∆: Pad by at least ∆ spaces. 
        p≤o.col: ''⍴⍨ ∆⌈ ¯1+ o.col- p        
          ''⍴⍨ ∆⌈ ¯1+ o.inc| p- o.col       
      }
      AT← (⌊0.5∘+){                         ⍝ AT: Generate Absolute col  
        0=⊃0⍴⍺: ⍺ ⋄ f← ⊃⍺                   ⍝ Fast-- col is a number      
          in out← ↓⍉↑(       
            '''[^'']*''' '&'
            '\s*⍝.*$'    ''
            '\s*$'       ''
          )
          LL← {                             ⍝ LL: Longest lines, length of w/ pctiles
              P← { i←100÷⍨p×¯1+≢⍵ ⋄ R 0.5× ⍵[⌊i]+ ⍵[⌈i] } ⍝ Pctile (rounded)
              R← ⌊0.5∘+                     ⍝ Round
              S← ⊂∘⍋⍛⌷                      ⍝ Sort 
            ⍝ 
              ⍺← 100                        ⍝ ⍺/p: What %age of ll. 
              p isB← ⍺ ⍺⍺                   ⍝ p: position, isB: 'best' option                              
              max← ⌈/ll← ≢¨in ⎕R out⊢ ⍵     ⍝ line lengths 
            ~isB: max 
              compact← max≤ o.compact 
              marg← isB+ compact⊃ 2⍴o.marg 
            compact: marg+ 1+ max           ⍝ Obj is compact, "best" is on the right.
            p≥ 100: marg+ R 0.01× p× max    ⍝ % (not %ile) if above 100% 
              marg+ P S ll                  ⍝ Actual interpolated percentile
          } 
          V←  ⊃∘⌽∘⎕VFI                      ⍝ Value
      ⍝ "Best" line length is  o.pctile-th %ile of input line lengths.
        f∊ 'bB': o.pctile (1 LL ) ⍵         ⍝ col set to "best" line length plus 1.
        f∊ '+-×': ((0 LL) ⍵) (⍎f) V 1↓⍺     ⍝ col is relative to exact max line length.
        0∊⊃⎕VFI ⍺: ⎕SIGNAL colÊ
          V ⍺                               ⍝ Absolute positioning
      }
      TB← { +/∧\' '= ⌽⍵ }                   ⍝ TB: Trailing blanks
      LB← { +/∧\' '=  ⍵ }                   ⍝ LB: Leading blanks 
      RF← {                                 ⍝ RF: Regex Field value
        ⍺.Lengths[⍵]↑ ⍺.Offsets[⍵]↓ ⍺.Block 
      } 
⍝ Main           
⍝ Preamble                    
      o.col← o.col AT ⍵                     ⍝ Calculate the absolute col pos'n.
      cur← 0                                ⍝ cur:     Our cur pos'n on this line.
      noCod← 1                              ⍝ noCod:   Just code on the line of ⍵?
      stI cdI lcI dblI cmI spI ← ⍳≢pats← (  ⍝ Our patterns...
        '^'                                 ⍝    stI: start    (of line)
        '''[^'']*''|[^⍝''\s]+'              ⍝    cdI:  code     (fragments)
        '\s*⍝\S.*$'                         ⍝    lcI: literal comment (don't format)
        o.dbl⊃ (                            ⍝    dblI: double comments
          '(*F)'                            ⍝    ← nop pattern, i.e. ignore                      
          '(\s*⍝.+?\s{5,})((?<!⍝)⍝(?!\S).*)$' ⍝    ← active pattern. ≥5 spaces between   
        )      
        '\s*⍝.*$'                           ⍝ cmI: comment  (w/ preceding spaces)
        '\s+(?!⍝)'                          ⍝ spI: spaces (not before comments)
      )
      DblCm← {                              ⍝ "Double" comments (see details)
        cm1 cm2← ⍵ RF¨ 1 2                  ⍝ ... get LHS and RHS comments
        cm1↓⍨← -TB cm1                      ⍝ ... Remove trail. blanks from LHS...
        pad← 5 AL cur+ ≢cm1                 ⍝ ... align "2nd" comment on RHS
        cm1, pad, cm2   
      }
    ⍝ Pattern matching scan 
      Executive← pats ⎕R {  
          m← ⍵.Match
          Case← ⍵.PatternNum∘=
        Case stI: m ⊣ cur⊢← 0  ⊣ noCod⊢← 1  ⍝ Start of line
        Case cdI: m ⊣ cur+← ≢m ⊣ noCod⊢← 0  ⍝ Code found
        Case lcI: m ⊣ cur+← ≢m              ⍝ literal comment '⍝⍝'
        Case spI: m ⊣ cur+← ≢m              ⍝ Spaces (not foll by comment)
      ⍝ Last two cases consume rest of line; cur is reset at stI above.
        Case dblI: DblCm ⍵                  ⍝ Double comment 
       ~Case cmI: ⎕SIGNAL logicÊ            ⍝ cmI: Default comments below ↓↓↓
          nsp← LB m                                        
        noCod∧ o.min> cur+ nsp: m           ⍝ If LHS comment, return as is
          m↓⍨← nsp                          ⍝ If RHS comment 
          m,⍨  1 AL cur                     ⍝ ... align at a valid col stop.
      }  
    ⍝ Main Executive
      Executive ⍵

  ⍝  Rest of "help" information
  ⍝H ---------------------------------
  ⍝H Other features:
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H ∘ Allows "double" comments, i.e. those with both
  ⍝H   a LHS comment (starting with ⍝) and a RHS comment (ditto). (See dbl: 1)
  ⍝H ∘ Can place comments in the "best" position, where some code lines
  ⍝H   are far longer than the average. (See col: 'best')
  ⍝H ∘ LHS comments are never moved.
  ⍝H ∘ RHS comments that start with ⍝⍝ or ⍝X, where X is any non-space, are never moved,
  ⍝H   even within "double" comments.
  ⍝H ∘ If the longest lines are shorter than ¨compact¨ number of bytes,
  ⍝H   (compact: 50) by default, the "best" position will be just to the 
  ⍝H   right of ALL lines.   (See compact and marg options).
  ⍝H ---------------------------------
  ⍝H right argument (⍵):
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H source:   'line1' 'line2' ... | 'Fn/Op Name' | 'File.typ' when (fi: 1)
  ⍝H   sourceDoc:   CVV  The source text to format. The updtd doc is returned.
  ⍝H   sourceFnOp:  CV   The name of a function or operator with the code to format; requires (fi:0).   
  ⍝H                     The updtd fn/op text is fixed and returned shyly.
  ⍝H   sourceFi:    CV   The name of a file with the code to format; requires (fi:1).  
  ⍝H                     It is updtd IN PLACE.
  ⍝H ---------------------------------
  ⍝H options (⍺):
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H   col:   target column in which to put right-hand side comments; 
  ⍝H          defaults to 'best', typically the 95th percentile on line lengths.
  ⍝H          See also min, inc.
  ⍝H   ----------
  ⍝H        col:   dd | '-dd' '+dd' '×d.dd' 'best' (or 'b'), where d is a digit.
  ⍝H        Format   Column value   Notes 
  ⍝H       'dd'|dd   col← dd        dd, an integer, here indicating exact column.
  ⍝H         '+dd'   col← ll+dd     ll, the length of the longest input line
  ⍝H         '-dd'   col← ll-dd     ll, the length of the longest input line
  ⍝H        '×d.dd'  col← ll×d.dd   d.dd, a small float/int string used to scale ll.
  ⍝H        'best'   col← pctile    dd is 1 past the dd-th percentile of input line lengths.
  ⍝H                                By default: (pctile: 95), the 95th percentile.
  ⍝H   inc:   If code text extends to <col> or beyond, place comments multiples
  ⍝H          of <inc> to the right of position <col>.
  ⍝H   min:   Treat any comments before column <min> as fixed LHS comments. 
  ⍝H          Defaults to 20.
  ⍝H   fi:    If 1 and ⍵ has depth ≤1, treats ⍵ as the name of a file to "tidy".
  ⍝H          Otherwise, a char vector right arg is treated as a fn or operator name.
  ⍝H          If ⍵ is a CVV (has multiple lines), fi is ignored.
  ⍝H   updt:  If 1 (default), will update fns/ops and files in place.
  ⍝H          If 0, the lines will be returned, but the object will 
  ⍝H          be unchanged.
  ⍝H   dbl:   If 1, will recognize pairs of comments on a line, 
  ⍝H            - the "first" will be treated as a LHS comment, and
  ⍝H            - the "second" will be aligned with the other RHS comments. 
  ⍝H            - The two must be have at least five blanks in between. 
  ⍝H          If 0, any comment is treated as either LHS or RHS comment.
  ⍝H   pctile: Unless (col: 'best') is set, pctile is ignored.
  ⍝H          If (col: 'best'), the default percentile length is used, 
  ⍝H          viz. (pctile: 95) plus 1.
  ⍝H          ∘ The pctile refers to the interpolated %ile of the length of all
  ⍝H            the lines in the input. 
  ⍝H            (Above 100%, a percentage above the longest line is used).)
  ⍝H          ∘ You can change pctile to any positive integer, where 
  ⍝H            100 is the 100th pctile, 90 is the 90%ile, and 120 is 120% of the max. 
  ⍝H   marg:  When (col: 'best') is used, marg specifies how much to separate 
  ⍝H          comments from the end of code. 
  ⍝H          Default: (marg: 2 5)
  ⍝H          ∘ The first number is used if code is NOT compact; 
  ⍝H            the second if it IS compact. 
  ⍝H          ∘ If the user specifies a single number, 
  ⍝H            it will be used for the current, i.e. both, col options.
  ⍝H          Compact code is defined as an object whose maximum line 
  ⍝H          length is smallish. See compact option.
  ⍝H  compact: Define width of code on line (incl. leading blanks)
  ⍝H          to be considered compact for the 'best' column option. 
  ⍝H          Default: (compact: 50).
  ⍝H          (compact: 0) means no object will be treated as compact.
  ⍝h          Only relevant if (col: 'best') is in effect.
  ⍝H ---------------------------------
  ⍝H Notes:
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H 1. If source is a char vector of vectors, it is treated as 
  ⍝H    multiline APL code (a fn, op, or set of code objects)
  ⍝H    a.  Returns the source with comments aligned per options.
  ⍝H 2. If source is a char. vector, and...
  ⍝H    a.  if (fi: 0), the default:
  ⍝H        - ⍵ refers to the name of a visible function;
  ⍝H        - its source representation (verbatim if possible) is formatted and...
  ⍝H          - returned as a shy value;
  ⍝H          - the function is also refixed for you. 
  ⍝H    b.  if (fi: 1):
  ⍝H        - ⍵ refers to a file, which is read;
  ⍝H        - its source is formatted and...
  ⍝H          - rewritten to the file (in place) and
  ⍝H          - returned as a shy value.
  ⍝H 3. Comments of course start with '⍝' (a lamp/comment sign).
  ⍝H    a) A comment starting with ⍝X, where X is any non-space, will never be moved.
  ⍝H    b) A double comment is a comment that contains two (or more) comment signs,
  ⍝H       of the form
  ⍝H        ⍝ Lefthand Side Comment           ⍝ Righthand Side Comment
  ⍝H    c) As per 3a) above, a LHS or RHS comment starting with ⍝ foll. by any 
  ⍝H       non-space will never be moved, as in this example:
  ⍝H        ⍝ Lefthand Side Comment     ⍝! This RHS Comment Will Never Move!
  ⍝H ------------------------------------
  ⍝H Documentation: 
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H   To see this information, call: Tidy⍨'help'  
  ⍝H
}
